= Programming language — Simple =

A '''programming language''' is a language for expressing instructions and ideas that a computer can use.

Examples include Python, C, JavaScript, Rust, Haskell, SQL, and many others.

Programming languages have rules about:

* how valid code is written — its '''syntax''';
* what that code means — its '''semantics''';
* how names and values work;
* how programs make decisions or repeat actions;
* how data is organized;
* which mistakes can be detected.

A language is not the same as the program that reads or translates it. One language can have several compilers or interpreters.

A [[Program (computing)/Simple|program]] is written in a language. Running that program causes [[Computation/Simple|computation]].

